---
// The last step of every project: pre-flight, the second save, and the honest stop at the fork.
// Run for the record on 17 September 2026 (cards/runs/2026-09-17/card-01-solidity.md).
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import StepCard from './StepCard.astro';
import StepPart from './StepPart.astro';
import SaveYourWork from './SaveYourWork.astro';
import StatusPill from './StatusPill.astro';
interface Props { n: number; message: string }
const { n, message } = Astro.props;
---

<StepCard n={n} title="Run pre-flight, and stop here">
  <StepPart kind="gets">
    <p>The same checks the deploy script will make, run before there is anything to lose.</p>
  </StepPart>
  <StepPart kind="do">
    <Code lang="sh" code="npm run preflight" />
  </StepPart>
  <StepPart kind="worked">
    <p>Six of seven checks pass. The one that fails is <code>DEPLOYER is a public address</code>, because you have not told the project which wallet you will sign with. That is the correct result here: the project ends at the fork.</p>
  </StepPart>
  <StepPart kind="ifnot">
    <p>Any other failure is real. The two about <code>.env</code> and key-shaped values mean a secret is tracked by git; fix that before anything else, and treat the secret as compromised.</p>
  </StepPart>
  <SaveYourWork when="again" message={message} />
  <p class="rb-stop"><StatusPill variant="pending" label="Testnet deploy: not part of this project yet" /> Deploying to testnet needs a verified wallet, and I have not run that step myself; <a href="/start/">Start here</a> says why and marks where it will go.</p>
</StepCard>

<style>
  .rb-stop { margin: 1rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; }
</style>
